thread:
anna: Heads up — onboarding sample app exposed a nasty ordering problem in the Node embed helper when partial retries occur. Rerank code assumes vectors are in input order.

ben: Oof. Node or Python helper?

anna: Node. We batch 3, chunking concurrent. If one item times out and we retry it solo, the retry can resolve before another chunk, so helper appends by arrival. Final vector order != input order.

kai: Minimal repro please?

anna: Items [p1,p2,p3,p4]. Chunks [p1,p2] and [p3,p4]. If p4 retries and returns before p3, helper returns [p1,p2,p4,p3].

ben: That's definitely an id->index reassembly bug. Helper must guarantee input-order. Quick patch: before sending build a map of {localReqId -> originalIndex} and write responses back into an output array at those indices.

kai: Or include a tiny envelope per item: {__idx, id, text} when calling client.embeddings.create so responses can be mapped. But server currently returns position-only arrays. Helper-side mapping is safer.

anna: Current helper snippet (simplified):

```js
// vulnerable: pushes arrivals
const results = [];
await Promise.all(chunks.map(async c => {
  try{ const r = await client.embeddings.create({input: c.map(i=>i.text)}); results.push(...r.data);} 
  catch(e){ for(const it of c){ const rr = await client.embeddings.create({input:[it.text]}); results.push(rr.data[0]); }}
}));
return results;
```

ben: Fix it to pre-allocate results = new Array(items.length) and when sending attach idx metadata so on response you do results[idx] = vector. Return results.filter(Boolean) or assert complete.

kai: Also add an opt-in `echo_ids` flag in SDK so server can return [{id, embedding}] for cases where apps prefer explicit envelopes. We'll default to false for perf.

anna: Good. I'll patch sample-app helper to preserve index mapping, add unit tests that randomly delay chunk responses, and update onboarding docs: "helpers guarantee input-order; do not rely on server sending ids unless echo_ids enabled."

ci-bot: ci/test-embed-helper queued: added unit test for index-preserving reassembly (simulated race).

ben: Follow-up: add optional per-item idempotency header so retries are deduped server-side when available. Also do a Node/Python parity pass; I think Python already handles this.

kai: Agreed. Thanks for catching this — would have caused subtle rerank mismatches in prod. :thumbsup:
